From: edk2-cix <edk2-cix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:51:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Silicon/CIX/Sky1: PciHostBridgeLib: report a missing I/O
 window as absent

Root bridges without an I/O aperture advertised a valid 0..0xFFFF I/O
window.  Nothing routes port I/O to PCIe (PcdPciIoTranslation is 0), so
a device's legacy I/O BAR could be placed at CPU physical address 0 with
I/O decode enabled.  Use Base > Limit as for the memory windows.

From Neol00/edk2-cix-unlocked V2.4.
---
 .../CIX/Sky1/Library/PciHostBridgeLib/PciHostBridgeLib.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Silicon/CIX/Sky1/Library/PciHostBridgeLib/PciHostBridgeLib.c b/Silicon/CIX/Sky1/Library/PciHostBridgeLib/PciHostBridgeLib.c
index 4ddf7586..569510d5 100644
--- a/Silicon/CIX/Sky1/Library/PciHostBridgeLib/PciHostBridgeLib.c
+++ b/Silicon/CIX/Sky1/Library/PciHostBridgeLib/PciHostBridgeLib.c
@@ -119,8 +119,13 @@ ConstructRootBridge (
     Bridge->Io.Base  = Appeture->IoBase;
     Bridge->Io.Limit = Appeture->IoBase + Appeture->IoSize - 1;
   } else {
-    Bridge->Io.Base  = 0;
-    Bridge->Io.Limit = 0xFFFF;
+    //
+    // No I/O aperture: use the "absent" convention (Base > Limit) like the
+    // memory windows.  A valid 0..0xFFFF window let PciBusDxe assign legacy
+    // I/O BARs (e.g. on discrete GPUs) at CPU physical address 0.
+    //
+    Bridge->Io.Base  = MAX_UINT64;
+    Bridge->Io.Limit = 0;
   }
 
   if (Appeture->Mem) {
